<title>FRANCE: Carrefour rises on GMB stake increase.</title>
<headline>Carrefour rises on GMB stake increase.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French retailer Carrefour firmed on Thursday after it said it had increased its stake in the GMB holding company which controls the Cora hypermarkets group, traders said.</p>
<p>Carrefour's latest move, which added 8.1 percent to a 33.34 percent bought on December 10, brings Carrefour nearer to control of GMB, an equity sales executive said.</p>
<p>The 3.1 billion francs Carrefour paid for the total 41.4 percent stake was not considered expensive, another source said.</p>
<p>Carrefour was up 2.72 percent to 3,205 francs at 1034 GMT.</p>
</text>
